title: Eurozone Bank Scare
subtitle: Panic spreads through Europe's banks...
new-page: true
on-arrival: banking_crisis_seen = 1; workers_linke += 3; workers_afd += 3; new_middle_afd += 3; old_middle_afd += 4; rural_afd += 3; unemployment_rate += 0.8; crisis_urgency += 1; workers_spd -= 3 if spd_in_government; new_middle_spd -= 4 if spd_in_government; old_middle_spd -= 4 if spd_in_government; rural_spd -= 3 if spd_in_government; economic_growth -= 1;
tags: event
view-if: recession_seen = 1 and time >= 15 and economic_growth < 0.5 and banking_crisis_timer = 0
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/danat_bank.jpg

= Eurozone Bank Scare

A large Italian bank has failed to raise fresh capital, and the yields on Italian and French government bonds are shooting up. Savers are queueing at branches in Milan and Marseille, and German banks with large holdings of southern European debt are seeing their shares collapse. Frankfurt is asking Berlin what it intends to do.

This is a crisis of the financial markets, but the bill will be sent to ordinary people, as it was in 2008.

- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @stabilization: Back the banks and push for a European rescue.
- @austerity: Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s answer is, once again, more austerity.
- @end_toleration: Enough austerity. We end our toleration of this government!

@nothing_to_do
view-if: spd_in_government = 1
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; trust_in_democracy -= 3

We leave the matter to the European Central Bank and hope that it holds.

@stabilization
view-if: spd_in_government = 1
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.5; budget -= 1; workers_afd -= 2; economic_growth += 0.8; west_relation += 1

Germany backs a joint European guarantee for bank deposits and recapitalises its own exposed banks. The markets calm down. It might not be enough, but the bleeding has stopped for now.

@austerity
view-if: spd_in_government = 0
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; trust_in_democracy -= 3; economic_growth -= 1;

Chancellor [+ chancellor +] responds to the bank scare by announcing more spending cuts to "reassure the markets".

@end_toleration
view-if: spd_toleration = 1
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_toleration = 0
call: set_next_election_time

We are tired of [+ chancellor +]'s austerity. When the government tries to push another round of cuts through the Bundestag, we vote it down together with the other opposition parties. The chancellor loses a vote of confidence, and the Federal President dissolves the Bundestag.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
